{
  "id": "Compound::DB08864 - Gene::1576",
  "verbalization": "Rilpivirine is linked to Cyp3a4 through a series of molecular interactions that involve non-nucleoside reverse transcriptase inhibitors (NRTIs) and organonitrogen heterocyclic compounds. The evidence suggests that Rilpivirine, as part of the Non-nucleoside Analog class, is included in the broader category of NRTIs, which in turn includes Etravirine and Nevirapine. These compounds all bind to Cyp3a4, a key enzyme in drug metabolism. The lowest common ancestors of Rilpivirine and its related compounds point to shared structural features, such as Aminopyrimidine and Organonitrogen Heterocyclic Compounds, which may contribute to their common mechanism of action. The integration of these pathways highlights a potential role for Rilpivirine in modulating Cyp3a4 activity, likely through shared pharmacological properties. The evidence supports a direct interaction between Rilpivirine and Cyp3a4, mediated by its inclusion in a class of drugs that share a common target.",
